# Allowlist, not a blocklist.
#
# Everything is excluded, and only what belongs in a release is allowed back in. The failure
# modes are not symmetric: a blocklist that misses a pattern publishes the file and nobody
# notices, while an allowlist that misses an entry leaves the file out of the repository, which
# is obvious the first time someone looks.
#
# Directories are re-included before their contents are excluded again - git cannot re-include a
# file whose parent directory is still excluded, so the order of these lines matters.
#
# Note that this only affects untracked files. Anything already committed stays committed.

/*

!/.editorconfig
!/.gitignore
!/LICENSE
!/README.md
!/*.lua

!/docs/
/docs/*
!/docs/api-notes.md

!/tools/
/tools/*
!/tools/check.sh

!/.github/
